---
layout: base.njk
title: "Give your agent a real Clash record"
description: "Elixir records Clash Royale history — battles, rosters, river races — and serves it to your own AI agent over MCP. Ask in plain language; the answer comes from the record, with the numbers behind it."
permalink: /index.html
canonical: /
navActive: home
---
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
{%- set lastDay = stats.series.battles_daily | last if stats.series and stats.series.battles_daily else null %}
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px; align-items: flex-start; padding-top: 24px">
  <div style="flex: 1 1 480px; min-width: 0">
    {#- The pill is baked from the daily series at deploy and says so by
        wording: "today" is the last day the series holds. -#}
    <span class="chip chip--ok" style="margin-bottom: 18px; display: inline-flex">
      <span class="chip__dot"></span>
      recording now{% if lastDay %} · {{ lastDay.battles | number }} battles recorded today{% endif %}
    </span>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Give your agent a real Clash record.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 24px; max-width: 50ch">
      Elixir records Clash Royale history — battles, rosters, river races — and
      serves it to your own AI agent over MCP. You ask in plain language; the
      answer comes from the record, with the numbers behind it.
    </p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 14px">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#request">Request access</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/quickstart">Connect your agent →</a>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote" style="margin: 0">
      Granted by hand while the corpus grows. Reading is universal — a tier only
      changes what we record for you.
    </p>
  </div>

  {#- The transcript replaces the counter panel here: a number says the
      corpus is big, an exchange says what it is FOR, and that is the
      argument the home page has to make. The counters sit below the
      fold, and /data is the page about how much there is. -#}
  <div style="flex: 1 1 440px; min-width: 320px">
    {%- set scripts = transcript %}
    {% include "transcript.njk" %}
    <p class="footnote" style="margin: 12px 2px 0">
      An illustration of a real exchange: every tool named under the window
      is in the registry and linked to its reference, and the citation under
      each answer is the kind this service actually returns. The numbers are
      illustrative; <a href="/data">the corpus</a> has the real ones.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="home-section" style="margin-top: 20px">
  <div class="home-section__head">
    <h2>What people use it for</h2>
    <a href="/use-cases/play" style="font-size: 13.5px">All 11 use cases ›</a>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-dim); margin: 0 0 20px">
    The chips above switch the conversation. Open one for the full walkthrough.
  </p>
  <div style="display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap">
    {%- set cases = [
      ["play", "/use-cases/play#play", "Understand your own play", "Which deck is actually winning, where your losses cluster, whether last month's change worked.", "reads your recorded battles and daily snapshots"],
      ["clan", "/use-cases/clan#clan", "Run your clan", "Who carried the race, who missed attacks, and who needs a word before the next one.", "reads war weeks past the API's 20-week window"],
      ["friends", "/use-cases/play#friends", "Follow your friends", "Track the people you play with — climbs, deck switches, heavy days, when you last teamed up.", "reads the players you chose to track"]
    ] %}
    {%- for c in cases %}
    <a class="case-card" href="{{ c[1] }}">
      <span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px">
        <span class="case-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- if c[0] == "play" -%}
          <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 7 13.5 15.5 8.5 10.5 2 17"/><polyline points="16 7 22 7 22 13"/></svg>
          {%- elif c[0] == "clan" -%}
          <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"/></svg>
          {%- else -%}
          <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        <span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink)">{{ c[2] }}</span>
      </span>
      <span style="display: block; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-body); margin-bottom: 10px">{{ c[3] }}</span>
      <span style="display: block; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-faint)">{{ c[4] }}</span>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <div class="home-section__head"><h2>How it works</h2></div>
  <div class="pipeline">
    {%- set steps = [
      ["Collectors fetch", "Volunteer machines poll the game's API on a schedule the hub sets, inside one shared request budget. They choose nothing; the server does.", "M6 8h12M6 12h12M6 16h8"],
      ["Elixir records", "Every payload is admitted once and kept: battles, rosters, snapshots, river races — including the weeks the API itself forgets.", "M4 6h16v12H4zM8 10h8M8 14h5"],
      ["Your agent reads", "Connect Claude, ChatGPT or any MCP client. It gets the tools, your entitlements, and every answer with its sample size.", "M12 3v18M3 12h18"]
    ] %}
    {%- for s in steps %}
    <div class="pipeline__step">
      <span class="pipeline__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="{{ s[2] }}"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span>
        <span style="display: block; font-size: 15.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 4px">{{ s[0] }}</span>
        <span style="display: block; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-dim)">{{ s[1] }}</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <div class="home-section__head">
    <h2>What it is reading</h2>
    <a href="/data" style="font-size: 13.5px">The corpus ›</a>
  </div>
  {#- The one place a number is gold on the home page: a brand moment
      on the marketing half, not a reading in the console. Baked at
      deploy from the same stats /data draws. -#}
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">battles</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.battles | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">{% if t %}since {{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}recorded{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">players</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.players | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">observed</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">clans</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.clans | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">observed</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">war weeks</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">recorded races</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section" style="display: flex; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap">
  <div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0">
    <div class="home-section__head">
      <h2>What&rsquo;s new</h2>
      <a href="/updates" style="font-size: 13.5px">All updates ›</a>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      {%- for u in updates.slice(0, 4) %}
      <a href="/updates#{{ u.date | truncate(7, true, "") }}" style="display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start; padding: 14px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft); color: inherit">
        <span class="mono" style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-faint); flex: 0 0 58px; padding-top: 2px">{{ u.date | replace("2026-", "") }}</span>
        <span>
          <span style="display: block; font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink)">{{ u.title }}</span>
          <span style="display: block; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-dim); margin-top: 2px">{{ u.body | clamp(140) }}</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1 1 260px; min-width: 0">
    <div class="home-section__head"><h2>For machines</h2></div>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
      <a class="machine-link" href="/api/public/stats">/api/public/stats</a>
      <a class="machine-link" href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>
      <a class="machine-link" href="/tools.json">/tools.json</a>
      <a class="machine-link" href="/feed.xml">/feed.xml</a>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote" style="margin: 14px 0 0">
      The tool list is generated from the registry, so it cannot drift from
      what the door actually serves: {{ tools.count }} tools across
      {{ tools.groups | length }} groups, at <code>{{ site.mcpUrl }}</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" id="request" style="margin-top: 20px; max-width: 560px">
  <div class="panel__head"><span class="panel-title">Request access</span></div>
  <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
    <div style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-faint)">
      Access is invite-approved while the recorder grows. Tell us who you are in the arena.
    </div>
    {#- The one interactive thing on the static half. Its script is
        /assets/request-form.js - an external file, not an inline
        block, because the CSP has no script-src 'unsafe-inline'
        (#25). Progressive enhancement is not available here (there
        is no non-JS POST target), so it fails loudly rather than
        silently swallowing a submission. -#}
    <form id="request-form" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
      <label>
        <span class="field-label">Email</span>
        <input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
      </label>
      <label>
        <span class="field-label">Your player tag</span>
        <input class="mono" name="player_tag" required placeholder="#20JJJ2CCRU" />
      </label>
      <label>
        <span class="field-label">Anything we should know? <span style="color: var(--ink-faint)">(optional)</span></span>
        <input name="note" />
      </label>
      <p class="field-error" id="request-error" hidden></p>
      <div><button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Request access</button></div>
    </form>
    <div class="notice" id="request-sent" hidden>
      If your request is approved, you&rsquo;ll hear from us by email.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="/assets/request-form.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/transcript.js" defer></script>
